Input: {"question": "Which award did Janina Bil receive?", "source_segments": {"D1S1": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 0, "end": 14, "text": "**Janina Bil**"}, "D1S2": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 16, "end": 163, "text": "Janina Bil was a Polish woman who risked her life to save Jews during the Holocaust, earning her the esteemed title of Righteous Among the Nations."}, "D1S3": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 164, "end": 193, "text": "**Early Life and Background**"}, "D1S4": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 195, "end": 251, "text": "Janina Bil was born in Poland in the early 20th century."}, "D1S5": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 252, "end": 390, "text": "Little is known about her early life, but it is evident that she was raised with strong moral values and a sense of compassion for others."}, "D1S6": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 391, "end": 430, "text": "**Rescue Efforts During the Holocaust**"}, "D1S7": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 432, "end": 517, "text": "During World War II, Bil lived in Warsaw, Poland, which was occupied by Nazi Germany."}, "D1S8": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 518, "end": 640, "text": "As the Nazis began their systematic persecution and extermination of Jews, Bil took it upon herself to help those in need."}, "D1S9": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 641, "end": 757, "text": "She provided shelter, food, and other essential resources to numerous Jewish families, often at great personal risk."}, "D1S10": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 758, "end": 879, "text": "One of the families Bil helped was the Goldberg family, who had been forced to flee their home and were living in hiding."}, "D1S11": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 880, "end": 994, "text": "Bil took them in, providing them with a safe place to stay and helping them to obtain false identification papers."}, "D1S12": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 995, "end": 1101, "text": "She also assisted other Jewish families, including the Rosenbergs and the Lewins, who were also in hiding."}, "D1S13": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1102, "end": 1148, "text": "**Recognition as Righteous Among the Nations**"}, "D1S14": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1150, "end": 1293, "text": "In recognition of her bravery and selflessness, Janina Bil was awarded the title of Righteous Among the Nations by the State of Israel in 1964."}, "D1S15": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1294, "end": 1398, "text": "This honorific title is bestowed upon non-Jews who risked their lives to save Jews during the Holocaust."}, "D1S16": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1399, "end": 1427, "text": "**Evidence and Testimonies**"}, "D1S17": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1429, "end": 1571, "text": "The Yad Vashem Holocaust Museum in Jerusalem, Israel, has documented Bil's rescue efforts and recognized her as a Righteous Among the Nations."}, "D1S18": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1572, "end": 1733, "text": "According to the museum's records, Bil's actions were verified through testimonies from the families she helped, including the Goldbergs, Rosenbergs, and Lewins."}, "D1S19": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1734, "end": 1880, "text": "In an interview with the Yad Vashem museum, Rachel Goldberg, one of the survivors Bil helped, recalled: \"Janina Bil was an angel sent from heaven."}, "D1S20": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1881, "end": 1933, "text": "She took us in, fed us, and gave us a place to stay."}, "D1S21": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1934, "end": 1975, "text": "Without her, we would not have survived.\""}, "D1S22": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1976, "end": 1990, "text": "**References**"}, "D1S23": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1992, "end": 2022, "text": "* Yad Vashem Holocaust Museum."}, "D1S24": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2023, "end": 2030, "text": "(1964)."}, "D1S25": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2031, "end": 2071, "text": "Righteous Among the Nations: Janina Bil."}, "D1S26": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2072, "end": 2084, "text": "* Gutman, Y."}, "D1S27": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2085, "end": 2092, "text": "(2007)."}, "D1S28": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2093, "end": 2184, "text": "The Encyclopedia of the Righteous Among the Nations: Rescuers of Jews During the Holocaust."}, "D1S29": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2185, "end": 2209, "text": "Yad Vashem Publications."}, "D1S30": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2210, "end": 2223, "text": "* Paldiel, M."}, "D1S31": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2224, "end": 2231, "text": "(2007)."}, "D2S1": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 0, "end": 157, "text": "As the sun set over the war-torn streets of Warsaw, Janina Bil made her way through the rubble-strewn alleys, her heart heavy with the weight of her mission."}, "D2S2": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 158, "end": 311, "text": "She had been working tirelessly with the Polish resistance, using her skills as a nurse to tend to the wounded and her bravery to smuggle Jews to safety."}, "D2S3": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 312, "end": 384, "text": "It was a dangerous game, one that could cost her her life at any moment."}, "D2S4": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 385, "end": 411, "text": "But Janina was undeterred."}, "D2S5": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 412, "end": 487, "text": "She had seen the worst of humanity, and yet she still believed in the best."}, "D2S6": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 488, "end": 660, "text": "She had lost count of the number of times she had risked her own life to save others, and yet she continued to do so, driven by a fierce determination to make a difference."}, "D2S7": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 661, "end": 737, "text": "As she turned a corner, she spotted a figure waiting for her in the shadows."}, "D2S8": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 738, "end": 849, "text": "It was Captain Jameson, a British officer who had been working with the resistance to coordinate their efforts."}, "D2S9": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 850, "end": 957, "text": "He was a tall, imposing man with a kind face and a sharp mind, and Janina had come to trust him implicitly."}, "D2S10": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 958, "end": 1020, "text": "\"Janina, I have some news,\" he said, his voice low and urgent."}, "D2S11": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1021, "end": 1075, "text": "\"The British government has taken notice of your work."}, "D2S12": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1076, "end": 1130, "text": "They want to recognize your bravery and selflessness.\""}, "D2S13": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1131, "end": 1161, "text": "Janina's heart skipped a beat."}, "D2S14": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1162, "end": 1222, "text": "She had never sought recognition, only to do what was right."}, "D2S15": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1223, "end": 1288, "text": "But Captain Jameson's words sparked a glimmer of hope within her."}, "D2S16": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1289, "end": 1352, "text": "Maybe, just maybe, this could be the turning point they needed."}, "D2S17": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1353, "end": 1373, "text": "\"What does it mean?\""}, "D2S18": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1374, "end": 1418, "text": "she asked, her voice barely above a whisper."}, "D2S19": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1419, "end": 1536, "text": "\"It means you'll be receiving the Distinguished Service Order,\" Captain Jameson replied, his eyes shining with pride."}, "D2S20": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1537, "end": 1601, "text": "\"It's one of the highest honors the British military can bestow."}, "D2S21": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1602, "end": 1652, "text": "You'll be the first Polish citizen to receive it.\""}, "D2S22": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1653, "end": 1717, "text": "Janina felt a lump form in her throat as she processed the news."}, "D2S23": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1718, "end": 1794, "text": "She thought of all the people she had helped, all the lives she had touched."}, "D2S24": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1795, "end": 1825, "text": "It wasn't about her, she knew."}, "D2S25": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1826, "end": 1896, "text": "It was about the cause, about the fight against oppression and hatred."}, "D2S26": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1897, "end": 2047, "text": "But as she looked at Captain Jameson, she saw the sincerity in his eyes, and she knew that this award was more than just a recognition of her bravery."}, "D2S27": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 2048, "end": 2184, "text": "It was a symbol of hope, a reminder that even in the darkest of times, there were still people who cared, who fought for what was right."}, "D2S28": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 2185, "end": 2270, "text": "And as she accepted the news, Janina felt a sense of pride and purpose wash over her."}}, "candidates": [{"candidate_id": "C0", "answer": "Righteous Among the Nations", "card_ids": ["d1:c0"]}, {"candidate_id": "C1", "answer": "Distinguished Service Order", "card_ids": ["d2:c0"]}], "original_cards": [{"doc_id": "d1", "card_id": "d1:c0", "entity": "award", "scope": "specific", "claim": "Janina Bil received the award of Righteous Among the Nations.", "answer": "Righteous Among the Nations", "quote": "In recognition of her bravery and selflessness, Janina Bil was awarded the title of Righteous Among the Nations by the State of Israel in 1964.", "original_document_number": 1}, {"doc_id": "d2", "card_id": "d2:c0", "entity": "award", "scope": "specific", "claim": "Janina Bil received the Distinguished Service Order.", "answer": "Distinguished Service Order", "quote": "\"It means you'll be receiving the Distinguished Service Order,\" Captain Jameson replied, his eyes shining with pride. \"It's one of the highest honors the British military can bestow. You'll be the first Polish citizen to receive it.\"", "original_document_number": 2}], "initial_answers": ["Righteous Among the Nations", "Distinguished Service Order"]}
